Follow https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/dc/dbb/tutorial_py_calibration.html

First, prepare a chessboard in front of the camera. Must be lit, 9x6

Use _calib_captureImageForCalib.py and dance the chessboard in front of the camera to capture a calibration image file. Make sure to select the correct camera in code, and Press Q to capture image. Images will be saved in a subfolder. Collect about 20 samples.

Then, run _calib_findCheckerboard.py on the captured images and make sure a checkerboard can be found in each image. Filter out bad images. (_calib_matchImagesInFolder.py is a helper script to do so)

After that, use _calib_calculateMatrix.py to calculate the intrinsic parameters. Copy to _calib_bestParams.py for record.

These params for each camera will be input into the camera-params.json for the main project
